er-windsurf.webp","alt","A purple 3D rhythm highway with four note lanes, score and combo panels, a track timer and keyboard prompts.","https://github.com/frankjniu/rhythm-game","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","GameMap local capture","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)","items",[80,81],"Windsurf","Claude model / chat","links","Related resources",[87],"resourceIds","section",{"_57":88,"_25":89},"Three.js","/resources/threejs/","Creator evidence",[93],"evidence",{"_57":94,"_25":95,"_96":97},"Read the author’s AI tools and prompt disclosure","https://www.linkedin.com/posts/frankniu_if-youre-not-vibe-coding-with-claude-sonnet-activity-7304977951761039362-2xQe","note","The creator identifies Claude Sonnet 3.7, describes passing output into Windsurf, and links the exact rhythm-game repository in the same post.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[102],{"_57":103,"_25":68,"_96":104},"Open the complete rhythm-game source","The full game is rhythm.html, with procedural music and geometry rather than a separate asset download. Third-party libraries load from CDNs. No repository code license is declared.","Access type","download","demo","Play or run",[110],{"_57":111,"_25":112,"_96":113},"Download and run Rhythm Master 3D","https://github.com/frankjniu/rhythm-game/archive/refs/heads/main.zip","No public hosted build was verified. Serve the downloaded directory and open rhythm.html. External CDNs supply Three.js and Tone.js, so internet access is needed; a click starts audio.","Game platform","Source download","Guide format","build log","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[121],{"_57":122,"_25":95,"_96":-7},"Read the creator’s build workflow","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[127,128,129,130],"Download the repository and serve its directory with a local HTTP server, then open rhythm.html.","Choose a track and difficulty, start the game, and use D/F/J/K as notes reach the target zone.","Test combo 